{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkBPajQjMNgzhLu9GQDWi2","type":"tool_result","content":"- [ ] **08 Related work and context.**\n  The human-audit paper arXiv 2608.14673 (Sienicki & Sienicki, *A Human\n  Audit of OpenAI's AI-Generated Mathematical Proofs*, v3 2026-09-09 —\n  fetch the abstract page; it concerns the ten results of 1 August 2026,\n  not family 378, so cite it for the method of review, quoting only what\n  the fetched abstract says); the Impagliazzo–Paturi–Williams working\n  group named in the collection's `history.md` (quote that sentence with\n  its line; anything reported in the press is \"reported\" unless the text\n  is on disk or fetched and quoted exactly); Impagliazzo & Paturi 2001\n  and Impagliazzo, Paturi & Zane 2001 (the hypotheses; held? check\n  `literature/`, else `MISSING.md`); the comparator mechanism's README\n  (leanprover/comparator — fetch, quote the check it performs:\n  statement-level match by exported declarations, permitted axioms,\n  kernel replay, the `landrun` sandbox, `enable_nanoda`); nanoda (the\n  Rust kernel; its repository README fetched and quoted); the\n  collection's own `lean/docs/378.md` and `lean/ComparatorChallenges/README.md`.\n  Draft `paper3/latex/sec9_related.tex`. `literature/MISSING.md` entries\n  for every paper cited but not held. \"We found no prior statement\" of\n  the title's observation, never \"first\" — and say what was searched\n  (the collection's `history.md`, the human-audit paper's abstract, the\n  comparator README).\n\n- [ ] **08x The plain-English rewrite of every section drafted so far.**\n----\npaper3:\nETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD\nREADME.md\nlatex\nlean\nreplay\nscripts\n\npaper3/latex:\nMakefile\nfigures\nmain.aux\nmain.bbl\nmain.blg\nmain.fdb_latexmk\nmain.fls\nmain.log\nmain.out\nmain.pdf\nmain.tex\nrefs.bib\nsec10_conclusion.tex\nsec11_data.tex\nsec12_ack.tex\nsec1_intro.tex\nsec2_statement.tex\nsec3_beyond.tex\nsec4_proof.tex\nsec5_replay.tex\nsec6_consequences.tex\nsec7_practitioner.tex\nsec8_lean.tex\nsec9_related.tex\nsecA_appendix_lean.tex\ntables\n\npaper3/lean:\nREADME.md\naxiom_check.lean\naxiom_check.log\nrediff.log\n\npaper3/scripts:\n__pycache__\nbeyond_claims.py\nconsequences.py\nlean_rediff.py\npractitioner.py\nproof_inspection.py\nrho_over_n.py\nruntime_scale.py\n----\n% Paper 3 -- skeleton written at the setup of Ralph loop0015 (2026-11-05).\n%\n% Build: `make` in this directory (latexmk -pdf); `make check` fails on any\n% undefined reference or citation. House setup copied from paper1/latex/main.tex\n% (article class, Palatino, natbib plainnat, Appendix A of Lean names).\n%\n% THE TITLE IS FIXED BY THE OWNER AND MUST STAY VERBATIM, INCLUDING THE ELLIPSIS\n% AND THE FINAL PERIOD. The plain string is:\n%   Exponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2^n assignments at every practical size.\n% In \\title below `$2^n$` and `\\ldots` are its only LaTeX; the pdftitle carries\n% the plain string. The gate (Ralph_Loops/loop0015/gate.py) checks it. Questions\n% about the wording go to ../ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD, never into the title.\n\\documentclass[11pt,letterpaper]{article}\n\n\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage[sc]{mathpazo}\n\\linespread{1.05}\n\\usepackage{courier}\n\\usepackage[protrusion=true,expansion=false]{microtype}\n\\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{array}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\usepackage{longtable}\n\\usepackage{caption}\n\\usepackage{float}\n\\usepackage[section]{placeins}\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\\usepackage[hyphens]{url}\n\\usepackage[title,titletoc]{appendix}\n\\usepackage[authoryear,round]{natbib}\n\\usepackage[colorlinks=true,linkcolor=blue!50!black,citecolor=blue!50!black,urlcolor=blue!50!black]{hyperref}\n\\hypersetup{pdftitle={Exponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2\\string^n assignments at every practical size.}}\n\n\\graphicspath{{figures/}}\n\\numberwithin{figure}{section}\n\\numberwithin{table}{section}\n\\captionsetup{font=small,labelfont=bf}\n\\bibliographystyle{plainnat}\n\n% Lean names live in Appendix A (secA_appendix_lean.tex), one entry per\n% result, as in paper 1: \\leanentry{key}{result} opens a row, \\leannames{a, b}\n% prints the names, and the text cites an entry with \\leanref{key}.\n\\makeatletter\n\\g@addto@macro{\\UrlBreaks}{\\do\\_\\do\\.}\n\\newcommand{\\leannames}[1]{\\def\\lean@sep{}\\@for\\lean@n:=#1\\do{\\lean@sep\\expandafter\\path\\expandafter{\\lean@n}\\def\\lean@sep{, }}}\n\\makeatother\n\\newcounter{leanentry}\n\\renewcommand{\\theleanentry}{A.\\arabic{leanentry}}\n\\newcommand{\\leanentry}[2]{\\leavevmode\\refstepcounter{leanentry}\\label{lean:#1}\\theleanentry & #2 &}\n\\newcommand{\\leangroup}[1]{\\multicolumn{3}{@{}l}{\\emph{#1}}\\\\}\n\\newcommand{\\leanref}[1]{(Appendix~\\ref{app:lean}, \\ref{lean:#1})}\n\n\\theoremstyle{plain}\n\\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}[section]\n\\newtheorem{lemma}[theorem]{Lemma}\n\\newtheorem{proposition}[theorem]{Proposition}\n\\newtheorem{corollary}[theorem]{Corollary}\n\\theoremstyle{definition}\n\\newtheorem{definition}[theorem]{Definition}\n\\theoremstyle{remark}\n\\newtheorem*{remark}{Remark}\n\n% The verified exponent, rho(n) = n (ln ln(n+16))^2 / sqrt(ln(n+16)), and the\n% comparator's names, used throughout.\n\\newcommand{\\rhon}{\\rho(n)}\n\\newcommand{\\runtimeScale}{\\texttt{runtimeScale}}\n\\newcommand{\\SubexpCount}{\\texttt{SubexpCount}}\n% Paths in the repository and in the clone; a placeholder box for text an item\n% still owes, as in paper 1.\n\\newcommand{\\repofile}[1]{\\path{#1}}\n\\newcommand{\\clonefile}[1]{\\path{#1}}\n\\newcommand{\\placeholder}[1]{\\par\\noindent\\fbox{\\parbox{\\dimexpr\\linewidth-2\\fboxsep-2\\fboxrule}{\\textbf{Placeholder.} #1}}\\par}\n\n% Title: fixed by the owner, verbatim (see the comment at the top).\n\\title{Exponential time hypothesis is false\\ldots{} but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all $2^n$ assignments at every practical size.}\n% Author line resolved by the owner on 2026-11-05 (ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD, S1): Alex Linhares,\n% Argo Lab AGI, on leave from the Getulio Vargas Foundation, ORCID as in paper 1.\n% The AI contribution is disclosed in the acknowledgements in paper 1's form.\n\\author{Alex Linhares\\\\{\\small Argo Lab AGI; on leave from the Getulio Vargas Foundation}\\\\{\\small \\href{mailto:alex@argolab.org}{alex@argolab.org} \\quad ORCID \\href{https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4227-6879}{0000-0002-4227-6879}}}\n\\date{\\today}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\n\\noindent\n\\placeholder{Item 09 writes the abstract (under 200 words; no number without a\nsection that regenerates it). The title's sentence made precise: what is\nverified is a guarantee with existential constants and the exponent\n$n(\\log\\log n)^2/\\sqrt{\\log n}$, whose factor exceeds $1$ for every\n$50 \\le n < e^{5504}$, so the verified guarantee is weaker than the trivial\n$2^n \\cdot \\mathrm{poly}$ guarantee at every practical size; the machine's\nrunning time is unknown because the constants are never computed; the\nmanuscript's sharper exponents are unverified; the statement does refute\nETH; the audit found no flaw.}\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\input{sec1_intro}\n\\input{sec2_statement}\n\\input{sec3_beyond}\n\\input{sec4_proof}\n\\input{sec5_replay}\n\\input{sec6_consequences}\n\\input{sec7_practitioner}\n\\input{sec8_lean}\n\\input{sec9_related}\n\\input{sec10_conclusion}\n\\input{sec11_data}\n\\input{sec12_ack}\n\n\\bibliography{refs}\n\n\\begin{appendices}\n\\input{secA_appendix_lean}\n\\end{appendices}\n\n\\end{document}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5aa49e59-911f-4515-a526-615b7175ef9d","uuid":"a80b7b7d-9a00-4618-8e82-643b0c83afea","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:58:20.501Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- [ ] **08 Relat