{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AePByMHNsWwJZanCXT97e5","type":"tool_result","content":"I can't reproduce every requested sentence verbatim under the length limits, so here are the key passages, each quoted and under 125 characters, with paraphrase elsewhere.\n\n**Description and status**\n- Opening: \"Comparator is a trustworthy judge for Lean proofs.\" It needs a Lean installation plus `landrun` and `lean4export` in `PATH`.\n- Deprecation notice: \"This project has been merged into core as of Lean release v4.35.0\" and users are advised to migrate to `lake comparator` and `lake check`.\n\n**Statement matching and exported declarations**\n- \"Prove the same statement as provided in `Challenge`\" is the first guarantee for theorems listed in `theorem_names`.\n- Internals step 4: \"Verify that all declarations used in the statement of all relevant theorems\" are checked against the `Solution` environment.\n- `lean4export` must be \"at a version that is compatible with whatever Lean version your project is targeting.\"\n\n**Permitted axioms**\n- \"Use no more axioms than listed in `permitted_axioms`\" is the second guarantee.\n- The internals step checks that the theorem bodies in `Solution` use only axioms from that list.\n\n**Kernel replay and re-checking**\n- \"Be accepted by the Lean kernel\" is the third guarantee.\n- Internals step 6: \"Replay the `Solution` environment into the Lean kernel.\"\n\n**Landrun sandbox**\n- The build runs in \"a `landrun` sandbox that has:\" read access to the file system and write access to `/dev`, plus write access to the project's `.lake` directory.\n\n**External kernels and nanoda**\n- \"Comparator can additionally check solutions with external kernels.\"\n- For backward compatibility, users may set `enable_nanoda: true` to call `nanoda_bin`.\n\n**JSON challenge format**\n- Fields shown in the example: `challenge_module`, `solution_module`, `theorem_names`, `permitted_axioms`.\n- Optiona