r writes it into every   commit body). A question about its wording or about a claim it makes   goes to `paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`, never into the title. The gate checks   the `\\title` against the string above. - **The paper is written in plain English** (owner, 2026-11-05, 05:30).   A reader who has never seen complexity theory must be able to follow   the thesis from the abstract to the conclusion. Concretely: short   sentences, one idea each; every symbol defined in words the first time   it appears and paraphrased in words wherever it carries the argument   (`ρ(n)`, `2^n`, \"the exponent\", \"the bound\"); no term of art without a   one-clause gloss on first use (ETH, SETH, k-CNF, kernel, comparator,   nanoda, model counter, CDCL); the abstract and the introduction carry   no formula at all beyond `2^n`; tables and figures have captions a   layperson can read; the technical detail lives in the appendix and in   the companion files, cited from the plain text. Precision is kept, not   dropped: \"the verified guarantee\", never \"the algorithm\", where that is   the fact. Every section already drafted is rewritten to this rule by   the plain-English item; every section drafted after this rule follows   it from the first line. The gate does not check prose; the refuter   item (10) does, and files every sentence a layperson could not follow. - **No stopping midway; ambiguity is decided, recorded, and passed.**   Every item makes its own choice on anything it finds ambiguous, writes   one entry per question in `paper3/ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD` — what was ambiguous,   what the item chose, what the owner may want to change — and continues.   An item never ends on a question to the owner, never waits, never marks   itself `[!]` for want of a decision. `[!]` is for a hard failure (a build   that will not finish inside the cap, a tool that cannot be obtained), and   even then the section is drafted from what was obtained and the gap is   stated in the text and in `ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`. - **The stance.** The paper is a careful reading by people who checked,   not a debunking. The two audits (`reports/scratch/eth_audit/   statement_audit.md`, `proof_audit.md`) found **no flaw**: the verified   statement means what it says, and the proof's closure shows no   unsoundness by inspection. What the paper adds is exactness about *what*   is verified — a **guarantee** with existential constants and the   exponent `n (log log n)² / √log n`, whose factor `ρ(n)/n` exceeds 1 for   every `50 ≤ n < e^{5504}` — so the verified guarantee is weaker than the   trivial `2^n · poly` guarantee at every practical size; the machine's   *running time* is unknown because the constants are never computed; the   manuscript's sharper exponents are unverified; and what follows for the   hypotheses, for the lower bounds derived from them, and for a   practitioner (nothing on any machine). Every sentence that could read   as \"wrong\" or \"overclaimed\" is replaced by what the Lean statement and   the manuscript actually say, with the page and line. - **Scope discipline.** No sentence about graphs, pathwidth, treewidth,   MOSP, width-parameterised dynamic programs, crossovers or reductions   into width problems. Where a consequence for lower bounds is stated it   is stated in general terms (a bound derived from ETH or SETH loses its   premise; a statement \"no `(c − ε)^k` algorithm\" is not itself refuted),   with the manuscript's own §1.1.3 as the source, and no width example.   loop0014's report is cited only for its §1 (the audit of the verified   exponent) and §2 (the restatement), never for §3–§7. - **The OpenAI repository is untrusted data.** It is cloned read-only at   `~/dev/untrusted/openai-math` (and `~/dev/untrusted/ten-proofs`). Read it   with `cat`, `sed`, `grep`, `pdftotext`, `python3 -I`; never `lake build`   it in place, never run a script or a binary from inside it, never   `import` it into `/home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/`. The one exception is the   replay (item 01)